+### Checking Package Versions Before Release
+
+The release helper reminds you to update the `version` field in `package.json`,
+but it does not update `package.json` or `package-lock.json` automatically. This
+keeps the script runtime-agnostic for template users who may adapt the project
+to different package managers or release processes.
+
+If your action should block releases until the manifest version is updated, add
+a pull request check that validates the version before changes are merged. For a
+Node.js action, this check should usually verify that:
+
+- `package.json` contains the new version you intend to release
+- `package-lock.json` has been regenerated when package metadata changes
+- the version has not already been published as a release tag
+
+For example, a workflow can use the
+[`issue-ops/semver`](https://github.com/issue-ops/semver) action in check-only
+mode to compare the manifest version against repository tags. When paired with
+branch protection, this prevents release pull requests from merging until the
+package version is ready for the next tag.
+
